{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Final rebar-debug report before Gerrit. Problem: first public MCP server construction emitted IncompleteFieldDefinitionWarning and aborted when that warning was an error. Proven root cause: MCP 1.29.0 leaves Settings.lifespan as an unresolved ForwardRef because Settings is defined before FastMCP and is never rebuilt after FastMCP exists; pydantic-settings 2.15 detects the incomplete FieldInfo on first Settings construction. Proof: direct upstream FastMCP reproduced without rebar; first versus second construction isolated process-global completion; pre-calling public Settings.model_rebuild returned True and removed the warning; dependency A/B and upstream issue 3294 ruled out rebar config, schemas, Starlette, and a new pydantic defect. Test: tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_settings_completion.py was final-form RED first in a clean subprocess, physically withheld from the fixer, GREEN afterward, and defect-seeded omission of model_rebuild returned it to the exact RED before restoration. Refactoring litmus passes because it observes only child exit and public server name. Fix: build_server lazily imports MCP v1 Settings beside FastMCP and calls Settings.model_rebuild before either HTTP or stdio construction; docs/env-vars.md was mechanically regenerated for the shifted source-line citation. Scope and safety: caller sweep found no consumer that depends on incomplete metadata or the warning; all rebar construction routes through build_server. The fix restores metadata completeness, adds no dependency or capability, preserves optional imports, and weakens no test. Validation: original warning-as-error node 1 passed; output-schema module 36 passed; stdio plus real HTTP lifecycle 2 passed; fresh-process original report exits 0 and prints rebar; make lint and make typecheck pass; full make test exits 0 with 13536 passed, 52 skipped, 289 deselected. Siblings: no second production FastMCP constructor; one direct constructor is test-only and excluded from the production construct sweep. Parity rule is that every rebar MCP server construction completes upstream Settings metadata before first stdio or HTTP construction; CLI, public facade, MCP tools, and automated callers all route through build_server; dual-direction is N/A. Residual warnings already owned: stumpy-cinnabar-basenji, treelike-unamusing-grosbeak, dragonish-sylphic-sheep, and unamicable-exuberant-chupacabra; accepted out of this fix with no duplicates. Plan advisory P6 remains accepted because the grouped preservation criterion is independently proven by the explicitly enumerated focused commands and the full suite."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786921493754596001,"uuid":"5d334af7-04c1-49fe-b481-96bd92074f59"}